  "model_authored_rationale": "TSP-320 solver: Or-opt + 2-opt local search with neighbour lists and don't-look\nbits, driven by iterated local search (double-bridge perturbation), compiled\nwith numba.\n\nRationale (unverified before measurement, but mechanically grounded):\nThe common reference builds a nearest-neighbour tour and then applies a\n*truncated* dense 2-opt (at most 300 improving moves, best-improvement over an\nO(n^2) gain matrix) with 24 random restarts.  For n=320 that truncation stops\nfar short of 2-opt local optimality and the neighbourhood contains no segment\n(Or-opt) moves, so its tours typically sit well above 2-opt+Or-opt quality.\n\nThis method replaces the search entirely:\n  * exact distance matrix, K=10 nearest-neighbour candidate lists,\n  * first-improvement 2-opt over candidate edges in both tour directions with\n    the standard d(a,c) < d(a,b) pruning and shorter-side reversal,\n  * Or-opt moves for segments of length 1..3, forward and reversed insertion,\n  * don't-look bits so re-optimisation after a perturbation is local,\n  * iterated local search with random double-bridge kicks, accepting only\n    improvements, run under a wall-clock budget shared evenly over the split.\nPer-instance time is derived from the split size so the whole split fits inside\nthe execution limit (development prediction happens inside the train limit, so\ntraining itself only warms the JIT and runs a short sanity check).\nNo labels are involved: the objective is computed directly from the instance.",
